<title>USA: US bill for tougher cigarette labeling planned.</title>
<headline>US bill for tougher cigarette labeling planned.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill to require tobacco companies to list all the ingredients, including any carcinogens, in their cigarettes will be introduced Tuesday, its sponsors said.</p>
<p>The bill would also require cigarette packs to carry stronger and bigger warning labels, Sen. Frank Lautenberg, D-N.J., and Reps. Marty Meehan, D-Massachusetts, and James Hansen, R-Utah, said in a statement.  They have scheduled a news conference Tuesday to announce details of the bill.</p>
</text>
